\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\title{From reflection generation to Pin and Spin}

\p{How does reflection generation lead to the Pin and Spin groups?
Starting with the Clifford algebra and its norm, we first lift orthogonal
transformations and use determinant parity to select the even carrier,
while the spinor norm measures the obstruction to normalization over a general
field. Field extension and explicit transvections then give concrete lifts
and examples of the obstruction.}

\p{Over local fields, finite-dimensional coordinates give the carriers their
topologies and let us study the Spin projection and its image. For rational
transformations, compatible compact-open reference subgroups provide the
prerequisites for passing from these local groups to the
\vocabk{restricted product}{fcap-004F} and its away and full adelic variants.}

\p{The \vocabk{rational diagonal}{fcap-004K} and the
\vocabk{finite adelic spinor norm}{fcap-004N} connect the rational and local
pictures. We then form the \vocabk{finite adelic class sets}{fcap-004P}
and compare them under \ref{fcap-004Q} enlargement and
\ref{fcap-004R} conjugation of the right subgroup, keeping the rational
left subgroup fixed. The final leaves return to the real Spin covers.}

